. Each body was in ‘fresh’ stage of decomposition when pre-placement samples were taken, and in ‘skeletonization’ stage when post-placement samples were collected, based on scoring of the gross morphological changes (
Megyesi et al., 2005
). The duration of each placement and the deposition context are reported in
Table 1
. The soft tissue was incised with a disposable scalpel, and a 12 V Dremel cordless lithium-ion drill with a diamond wheel drill bit was used at max. 5000 revolutions to collect ~1 cm
3
of bone. Sampling instruments were cleaned with bleach and deionized water between each individual sample collection.
